ADDITIONAL INFORMATION
This worksheet is intended to assist in organizing financial information necessary for bankruptcy preparation.
Federal law requires that debtors receive credit counseling from an approved provider within 180 days prior to filing a bankruptcy petition.
In certain circumstances, a Reaffirmation Agreement may be required for secured debts that the debtor intends to continue paying following bankruptcy. Such agreement is executed between the debtor and creditor to exclude specific debts from discharge.
The United States Bankruptcy Court prescribes required disclosures and documentation for reaffirmation agreements. Consultation with a qualified attorney is strongly recommended for guidance.

